B.a1J=new A.f5("1 \xb7 final vs const","final = decided once at run time. const = decided at compile time, and canonicalised (identical consts share one object). Widgets love const: it lets Flutter skip rebuild work.","final now = DateTime.now(); // runs now\nconst pad = 16.0;           // known forever")
B.a1T=new A.f5("2 \xb7 Null safety (?, ??, !)","Types are non-nullable by default. A trailing ? allows null; ?. calls only if non-null; ?? supplies a fallback. ! asserts non-null \u2014 the compiler trusts you, the runtime may not.","String? name;                    // may be absent\nfinal len = name?.length ?? 0;   // safe chain + fallback")
B.a1Q=new A.f5("3 \xb7 Arrow functions","One expression, no braces. Callbacks everywhere in Flutter are arrows: onPressed, builders, map(). If it needs two statements, use a block.","onTap: () => select(i),\nfinal doubled = items.map((e) => e * 2).toList();")
B.a1K=new A.f5("4 \xb7 Spread + collection-for",'... unpacks a list inline; for() inside a literal builds UI lists declaratively. Most "dynamic children" code in this library is one of these two lines.',"final all = [...a, ...b];\nchildren: [for (final t in ts) Tile(t)],")
B.a1N=new A.f5("5 \xb7 Classes in one sip","final fields + generative constructor. const constructor when all fields are final \u2014 like every model in core/data.dart.","class Tx {\n  const Tx(this.title, this.amount);\n  final String title;\n  final double amount;\n}")
B.a1P=new A.f5("6 \xb7 async / await","await pauses THIS function, never the UI. The chat reply, the fake loading skeleton and the music ticker all lean on this.","final res = await fetch();   // UI stays alive meanwhile\nFuture.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 1), reply);")
B.a1R=new A.f5("7 \xb7 String interpolation","Stick $variable or ${expression} inside a string. That is how every amount, count and label in this library is formatted.","'Balance: $amount';")
B.a1U=new A.f5("8 \xb7 Control flow","if/else for branches, for-in for iterating, switch for many-way choices. The drawer, the rail and every list in this app are for-ins in disguise.","if (loggedIn) {\n  showHome();\n} else {\n  showLogin();\n}\nfor (final t in ts) {\n  print(t);\n}")
B.a1V=new A.f5("9 \xb7 Functions & named parameters","Positional params for the required core, {named} for options. required marks must-pass options; = gives defaults. Nearly every Flutter widget constructor works exactly like this.","Widget tile({required String title, bool active = false}) {\n  return ListTile(title: Text(title), selected: active);\n}")
B.a1O=new A.f5("10 \xb7 Lists & Maps","List = ordered, index by number. Map = keyed, index by key. <String> and <String, int> are type arguments: they tell the compiler what the collection holds so mistakes fail fast.","final names = <String>[]; // typed empty list\\nnames.add('ada');          // grow it\\nfinal scores = <String, int>{'ada': 42};\\nscores['bob'] = 7; // Maps work the same way")
B.a1M=new A.f5("11 \xb7 Imports: packages vs files","package: imports come from dependencies (pubspec). Relative imports are your own files. The rule: never import across packages with ../ \u2014 depend on it properly instead.","import 'package:flutter/material.dart'; // a package you depend on\\nimport '../core/tokens.dart';           // your own file, relative")
B.a1L=new A.f5("12 \xb7 main() & runApp()","main is where execution starts; runApp inflates the widget tree and attaches it to the screen. lib/main.dart in this project is two lines \u2014 everything else is widgets.","void main() {\n  runApp(const CounterApp()); // inflate the tree\n}")
B.a1I=new A.f5("13 \xb7 The widget tree (read inside-out)","A Flutter UI is widgets inside widgets. Read it inside-out: content at the center, layout around it, page frame outside, app outside that. Every demo page in this library has this exact shape.","MaterialApp(      // theme + navigation\\n  home: Scaffold( // page frame\\n    body: Center( // layout\\n      child: Text('Hi'), // content\\n    ),\\n  ),\\n);")
B.a1S=new A.f5("14 \xb7 State & setState in 3 lines","StatelessWidget = no memory, pure function of inputs. StatefulWidget + State = memory that survives rebuilds. setState marks the widget dirty; Flutter re-runs build() and the UI reflects the new values.","int count = 0; // the memory, lives in State\nvoid bump() => setState(() => count++); // write + mark dirty\nText('$count'); // build() reads the variable")
